AFAIK there is no need to have a fallback, spreading a variable that is `undefined` results in an empty object:

```js
var a = undefined
var b = { ...a }
a // {}
```

```suggestion
  var renderOptions = { ...this.locals, ...opts._locals, ...opts };
```

